The investigation identified a Registry modification associated with the Windows Event Log service.

4. Registry Command Identified

The following command was observed:

REG ADD HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\EventLog /t REG_DWORD /v Start /d 4

This command uses the Windows REG utility to modify a Registry value.

Command Breakdown
Parameter	Description
REG ADD	Adds or modifies a Registry value
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE	System-wide Windows Registry hive
SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\EventLog	Registry path for the Event Log service
/t REG_DWORD	Specifies the Registry value type
/v Start	Specifies the Start value
/d 4	Sets the value to 4
5. Finding

The command modifies the Start Registry value associated with the Windows Event Log service.

The value was changed to:

Start = 4

A Windows service Start value of 4 represents a Disabled startup configuration.

Therefore, the command was used to configure the Windows Event Log service as disabled.

