7. Security Impact

The Windows Event Log service is responsible for collecting and managing Windows event logs.

Disabling this service can reduce the availability of security and system telemetry. This may impair monitoring and make investigation of subsequent activity more difficult.

The behavior is therefore relevant from a Defense Evasion perspective.

8. MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
T1562.001 – Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools

Observed behavior:
A Registry modification was used to set the Windows Event Log service's Start value to 4, configuring the service as disabled.

Purpose/Impact:
This can impair security logging and reduce defensive visibility on the affected system.

