10. Overall Activity

The REG utility was used to modify the Registry configuration of the Windows Event Log service. The Start value was set to 4, which configures the service as disabled.

This activity is consistent with Defense Evasion – T1562.001 (Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools) because disabling the Event Log service can impair logging and security monitoring.

11. Conclusion

The investigation identified an attempt to disable the Windows Event Log service through a Registry modification.

The command:

REG ADD HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\EventLog /t REG_DWORD /v Start /d 4

changed the service's Start configuration to 4 (Disabled).

The activity represents a security-relevant modification that can reduce Windows logging and defensive visibility and is mapped to MITRE ATT&CK T1562.001 – Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools.
